            <ArticleTitle>Ankle arthroscopy in the adolescent patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>510-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author reviews 15 cases of ankle arthroscopy in adolescent patients. Most of the patients were female. He discusses the various pathologies identified, with the most common being a medial impingement lesion. Synovitis was present in all cases of persistent discomfort.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
